# packages/Brewfile.local.example - copy to Brewfile.local (same directory) and edit:
#     cp packages/Brewfile.local.example packages/Brewfile.local
# Untracked and never committed. It is bundled AFTER the tracked
# packages/Brewfile (`brew bundle`), for THIS host's extra picks.
#
# The split is deliberate: the tracked Brewfile carries the tools the framework's
# own tracked config depends on (each noted with its `# config/<prog>`), plus the
# CLI floor every host should always have. GUI casks, Mac App Store apps, language
# toolchains and one-off experiments belong HERE - they are personal, they churn,
# and a cask that fails to install should never break another machine's provisioning.

# brew "go"
# brew "awscli"
# cask "visual-studio-code"
# cask "1password-cli"
# mas "Amphetamine", id: 937984704

# Arch-specific formulae use on_arm / on_intel blocks:
# on_arm do
#   brew "an-apple-silicon-only-tool"
# end
